# Translation CSVs must stay LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# These files are edited by scripts as often as by hand, and Python's
# csv.writer emits CRLF unless told otherwise. When a file's endings did not
# match what a script wrote, the whole file was rewritten and the real change
# vanished into a full-file diff. Normalising here makes that class of noise
# impossible rather than something each script has to remember.
#
# `-text` is deliberate: it disables git's own eol conversion, so a Windows
# checkout also gets LF and cannot silently reintroduce CRLF on commit.
*.csv   -text
*.py    -text
*.md    -text
*.json  -text
